{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n '\"'^## (7|8|10)|Base64 seam|''^#|chunk|Chunk'\"' docs/design/dao.jing.dht.md docs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md docs/agents/build-n-test.md /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790762091000-orchestrator-dao-jing-dht-epic-owner-decisions.md\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790762091000-orchestrator-dao-jing-dht-epic-owner-decisions.md:4:# dao.jing.dht epic — OWNER DECISIONS (verbatim), after mob synthesis + ratification\n/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1790762091000-orchestrator-dao-jing-dht-epic-owner-decisions.md:8:remote-destination keys; S3 acceptance criterion \"shared chunk utility used by both\" with a declared DHT-owned-reassembly\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:5:# BUILD & TEST\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:7:## Commands\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:10:# Tests (Babashka runner)\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:17:# ClojureScript / shadow-cljs (always via deps.edn :cljs alias, never npx)\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:22:# ClojureDart\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:25:# Linting\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:36:## Testing Philosophy & TDD\ndocs/agents/build-n-test.md:49:## Debugging Malformed CLJ / EDN / CLJS\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:1:# DaoJing DHT: Content-Addressed Segment Distribution\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:10:## 1. Overview and scope\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:40:## 2. Layering and composition\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:99:## 3. The stream API\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:146:## 4. Writes: local insert, then acknowledged when sent to multiple peers\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:154:### 4.1 What the acknowledgement asserts\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:162:  the message, chunks included. A peer for which any datagram answered\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:178:### 4.2 Two entry points, one pending write\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:195:### 4.3 How a write proceeds, and what the caller sees when it cannot\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:244:### 4.4 Publication (owner decision 1)\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:261:### 4.5 Reads\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:279:## 5. The `dao.jing` adapter, the JVM facade, and time\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:281:### 5.1 The byte-store handle (owner decision 4)\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:303:### 5.2 The JVM blocking facade\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:312:### 5.3 Time\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:325:## 6. Peers and routing\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:356:## 7. The wire (v1)\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:386:;; chunk\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:388: :op :chunk :q n :dir :request | :reply\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:397:- Payload and chunk bytes are CBOR byte strings on the wire. Base64 appears\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:405:- **Chunks.** A message whose encoding exceeds the datagram budget is sent as\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:406:  `:chunk` records, each fitting the budget. Reassembly is keyed\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:413:  chunk is sent**.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:420:## 8. Hardening\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:427:  echoes it in every later request and request chunk to that peer. A cookie\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:443:- **The gate.** A request or request chunk without a valid cookie causes no\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:458:  `:find`, `:store`, `:fetch` or a chunk to a peer it holds no cookie for.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:467:- **A request chunk is verified before any partial state is allocated**, and\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:470:- **Reply chunks** are accepted only for a pending query to that observed\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:479:## 9. Limits and defaults\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:497:## 10. Today's code, and the slices that replace it\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:509:### Slice plan\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:515:**Base64 seam.** The format is one: padded standard-alphabet Base64, strict.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:544:`cookie-for`. Chunks are S3; the keyed MAC is S4. Acceptance:\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:564:**S3 — real sockets and chunks.** Depends on S1 and S2. Chunk records and\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:570:  chunks stay within every bound.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:571:- A chunked write counts a peer only when every chunk answered `ok`.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:572:- **One transport-neutral chunk split/absorb utility is used by both\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:583:`cookie-for` replacing the S2 stand-in, the chunk path under the gate, and\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:588:  Tested across datagram sizes from 1 byte to the budget, chunks included.\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:612:## Relationship to the intake-pool observer\ndocs/design/dao.jing.dht.md:622:## Lineage\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:1:# DaoStream Datagram: The Raw Datagram Layer\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:8:## 1. Place in the stack\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:20:       └─ dao.jing.dht          Kademlia wire, chunks, hardening (dao.jing.dht.md)\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:34:## 2. Values\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:81:(`dao.jing.dht.md` section 10, Base64 seam).\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:83:## 3. The socket, its identity and its descriptor\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:127:## 4. The writer handle\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:173:## 5. The traffic stream\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:190:## 6. Peer observers on one socket\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:207:## 7. `dao.stream.udp` rebuilt on this layer\ndocs/design/dao.stream.datagram.md:232:## 8. Exposure\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
